  "measurement_boundaries": {
    "comparison": "No matched performance inference against Delugi, Raptr, or Mysticeti: process model, input batching, duration, latency aggregation, and traffic boundaries differ. These are native functional smokes, not saturation or ranking experiments.",
    "throughput": "Native committed transaction count is summed across workers within each authority, then maximum across authorities, divided by integer elapsed seconds. Replicated authority counts are not summed.",
    "latency": "Native client transaction UTC timestamp to locally materialized ordered payload; mean is weighted by observations across worker replicas. Native reported observation count is maximum worker count, not the pooled denominator.",
    "percentiles": "Native p50 and p99 are medians of per-worker percentile values; one worker per authority here. They are not pooled transaction percentiles or an all-replica completion barrier.",
    "traffic": "Native sent/received counters summed across primary and worker registries; includes same-authority primary-worker traffic, and receive totals include client ingress. Framing/authentication/ACK boundaries differ from successful replica TCP stream-write accounting in the matched Delugi matrix.",
    "window": "First SUMMARY and its single BENCHMARK_RESULT line after warmup. Later STEADY-STATE diagnostic drain output is excluded. Native duration truncates elapsed time to whole seconds.",
    "backlog": "Native saturating submitted-minus-maximum-committed count at the measurement boundary; not an arrival-cohort drain or full agreement proof.",
    "agreement": "Native useful progress, nonzero workload/network counters, zero reported panics, and process exit zero; no independent full executed-prefix agreement check.",
    "cleanup": "All five run-owned native processes exited naturally with status zero; no surviving owned Vantage processes were observed."
  },
